Package: r4agent
Title: Benchmark AI Agents and Language Models Against Your Own Cases
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pawan Rama", "Mali", email = "prm@outlook.in",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")))
Description: Runs an agent or language model against a fixed suite of cases and
    reports whether it is ready for production. Cases carry an expected answer,
    a slice, and a severity. Results are graded locally, emitted as 'R4SUB'
    evidence rows through 'r4subcore', scored per slice against thresholds
    agreed before the run, and compared against a previous run so that a case
    which used to pass and now fails is visible rather than averaged away.
    Grading is deliberately deterministic and offline: no model is called to
    judge another model, which keeps a benchmark reproducible and free.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    r4subcore,
    cli,
    jsonlite,
    stats,
    utils
